        "topic_deep_dive": "Gradient descent has several variants that differ in how many training examples are used to compute the gradient at each update step. Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD) uses a single training example per update, making it fast but noisy. Mini-batch gradient descent uses a small subset of the training data, balancing computational efficiency with gradient stability. Full-batch gradient descent uses the entire dataset, which is more accurate but computationally expensive. The choice among these variants affects both the speed of training and the quality of convergence.",
