        "topic_deep_dive": "Momentum is a technique used to improve the efficiency of SGD by incorporating information from past gradient updates. Instead of updating parameters based solely on the current gradient, momentum accumulates a velocity vector in directions of persistent descent, effectively smoothing out the update trajectory. This helps the optimizer move faster through flat regions of the loss landscape and reduces oscillation in directions where the gradient frequently changes sign. Momentum is particularly useful when the loss landscape has narrow valleys or when gradients are noisy, as is common in SGD.",
