        "topic_deep_dive": "Regularization is a technique applied during optimization to prevent overfitting, which occurs when a model learns the training data too well and fails to generalize to new data. The teaching content describes L1 and L2 regularization as methods that penalize large weights during the optimization process. By adding a penalty term to the loss function, these techniques discourage the model from assigning excessively large values to its parameters. L1 regularization tends to produce sparse weight vectors, while L2 regularization encourages smaller but non-zero weights. Both are applied during training as part of the optimization objective.",
